bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_lowering_error_names_entry_file_not_defining_module_2026-11-26, 0, "A lowering type error raised inside an IMPORTED module is reported against the ENTRY file. Repro: m2a.spl = use m2b.{z} + main; m2b.spl = pub fn z() -> text: d.get(\"k\") on a Dict<text, text>. compile m2a.spl prints: declared return type mismatch in function z (m2a.spl) ... and compile failed (m2a.spl). The function line (function at line N / return at line N) then points into the wrong file. During the sweep the defining file had to be found with strace (std.sys.env get resolved to src/compiler_rust/lib/std/src/sys/env.spl:17). Expected: the message names the defining module path. eprintln site: src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/hir/lower/module_lowering/function.rs (self.current_file is the entry file while imported functions lower)."

